Trees","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","scores.prefixSum(through: 3)        \/\/ 9","scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6)             \/\/ 19","scores.add(10, at: 1)","scores.lowerBound(ofPrefixSum: 15)  \/\/ 2"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A Fenwick tree’s update tree, in which each cell’s parent is the next cell an add reaches,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converts to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (import Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module beside this one), so Grafluent’s tree algorithms and drawings run over it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" combines any range of values under a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Monoid","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": an associative operation with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an identity, written as a type such as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Sum","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/Minimum","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or one of your own, which need not be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"commutative. Range queries and point updates take O(log ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"text":"), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree\/maxRight(from:where:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree\/minLeft(upTo:where:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" find how far a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range can grow while a monotone condition on it holds.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var heights = SegmentTree<Maximum<Int>>([3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6])","heights.combined(in: 0 ..< 4)        \/\/ 4","heights.update(at: 1, to: 7)","heights.maxRight(from: 0) { $0 < 9 } \/\/ 5"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" also applies an update to every value in a range in O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), leaving it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pending at the cells that cover the range. A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" names the monoid, the updates and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"how an update changes a combined value; it is told how many values the combination covers, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"adding a constant to a range of sums is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sum + update * count"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" holds half-open intervals with a value each, in an AVL tree ordered by lower","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bound whose vertices also record the largest upper bound below them. It finds the intervals that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contain a point, overlap a range or lie within one, skipping every subtree that e